[meta]
title = "PAXAI STORAGE LIFECYCLE PREREQUISITE — CANDIDATE PROFILE 1"
version = "1"
status = "PROFILE_IMPLEMENTATION_APPROVAL_AND_QUALIFICATION_UNRUN"
canonical_spec = "../../spec.kvx"
task_authority = "Canonical ai.* tasks and requirements are defined in ../../spec.kvx."
qualification = "functional specification; implementation and qualification UNRUN. Native implementation, profile approval, build, behavior qualification, archive recovery and continuous-operation release are UNRUN. This contract supplies a concrete bounded candidate and explicit activation decisions; it does not authorize protocol activation. It complements core.kvx C07 and integration-map.kvx I02. Actual canonical blob deletion is a consensus state transition and produces a new root. Historical roots and their proof validity must remain unchanged in retained historical material."

[storage.S01]
title = "TWO INDEPENDENT STORAGE BOUNDS"
paragraph_001 = "PAXAI application state has one program-shared key paxai/state/v1 and at most196608 bytes. This limits the serialized current application object, not the number of historical native content objects. Each distinct state version generally creates a content value and a manifest even though the guest writes one key. Repeated identical content may deduplicate, but deduplication cannot be the capacity plan for changing state."
paragraph_002 = "The current native kernel has512 committed blob slots,67108864 committed blob bytes,1048576 bytes per blob, and4 staged blob entries per activity. Deletion entries also consume staged slots. Native module KV has512 entries and64 staged writes per activity. Program replay capture, when enabled/present on the real path, adds an activity-specific replay KV record and one witness blob. Artifact, migration, oracle/web and sandbox state share native capacity. The app's two content blobs are therefore an application contribution, not a whole-transaction guarantee of two total blobs."
paragraph_003 = "A one-key manifest contains the version/count prefix and one key/digest/length entry. For paxai/state/v1, the key is14 ASCII bytes and the manifest is58 bytes. At maximum app size, its pair adds196666 bytes before optional replay witness and other native evidence. The upper bound on isolated mutation count with no reclamation is bounded both by slots and bytes; floor(512/2)=256 is only an empty-store upper bound, not an available quota or certified number of calls. Replay and existing occupancy can reduce it materially."
paragraph_004 = "Neither the four-market pilot policy nor32 completed app epochs creates more native capacity. App epoch pruning, shared key deletion and namespace drop must never be reported as native physical reclamation without actual native accounting evidence."

[storage.S02]
title = "CANONICAL CONTENT IS STATE, NOT A DISPOSABLE CACHE"
paragraph_001 = "Every current native blob contributes a leaf to its module subtree using its exact content bytes and digest-derived leaf key. A blob remains committed state even when no currently visible namespace head refers to it. Removing it changes the module root and resulting state root. Local cache timing must never alter these canonical sets."
paragraph_002 = "Current lxp_ctx_blob_del is a staged canonical deletion primitive. It can be used only from an admitted deterministic module transition with exact authority, root binding, rollback and replay behavior. A background thread, process restart, disk quota cleanup, local archive upload, local finality observation or local reachability scan must not directly alter kernel->blobs, count, total bytes or root."
paragraph_003 = "Existing sandbox-destroy reclamation is a narrow implementation path, not a general shared-state collector. Its reference scan recognizes73-byte storage-head keys and omits the41-byte program-shared head form. Its assumptions about paired lease heads do not apply to shared PAXAI state. The implementation must not reuse that helper unchanged, and this prerequisite does not authorize a neighboring repair to unrelated sandbox behavior. New shared-safe reference handling must be separately scoped and qualified; the narrow helper limitation remains a constraint."

[storage.S03]
title = "SAFE IMMEDIATE OPERATING PROFILE"
paragraph_001 = "Until the candidate lifecycle is approved and qualified, only a finite-capacity profile is admitted. Its release manifest declares NO_CONTINUOUS_OPERATION, observed native counts/bytes at a specific committed sequence/root, actual call overhead and an absolute bounded mutation budget below remaining headroom. The operator stops admitting new market mutations before that budget is exhausted and preserves canonical snapshots, logs, receipts, proofs and liabilities. All existing pending economics continue to reconcile; a stop on new work must not erase payout/exit obligations."
paragraph_002 = "The finite profile may be used for explicitly bounded development/qualification experiments. It must not advertise indefinite operation, automatic GC or successful production continuity. It requires enough reserved native headroom to finish already admitted terminal/claim/exit operations. If that reserve cannot be demonstrated, no new funded epoch is admitted. A read-only app query is also not presumed free of native replay/fee overhead; measure its real path before counting it as nonmutating capacity consumption."

[storage.S04]
title = "MINIMAL CONTINUOUS-OPERATION CANDIDATE"
paragraph_001 = "Candidate profile1 uses a versioned deterministic Programs maintenance activity to retire narrowly identified obsolete Programs content and old replay records after complete authenticated historical archival. It retains native module ID9, existing state-leaf/hash formats, current blob/KV bounds, transfer law, snapshot serialization and proof encodings. It adds no guest blob-delete host function and grants no application owner arbitrary native deletion authority."
paragraph_002 = "The proposed integration point is a new Programs module version with a storage-retirement activity. The currently unused next ordinal11 under module9 is a candidate allocation, not an existing API or approved numeric assignment. Registry version, activity catalogue, decoder, authority resolver, replay dispatcher, SDK transport and candidate manifest must agree before use. Existing historical module versions continue to replay under their old semantics. No old recorded activity is reinterpreted as cleanup."
paragraph_003 = "The maintenance transition changes canonical state through the normal kernel prepare/commit/journal/batch path. It emits a bounded receipt-backed cleanup outcome carrying old root/new root, profile digest, candidate-set digest, removed object identities/count/bytes, retired replay-record identities and archive certificate digest. The new root is expected and must match independent replica replay. Existing historical root bytes, proof paths, receipt digests and checkpoint identities are not rewritten."
paragraph_004 = "This is a platform prerequisite, not one of the ten app features. If protocol owners do not approve the new versioned maintenance profile, the safe result is the finite profile of S03; do not substitute background deletion or raise limits."

[storage.S05]
title = "PROFILE IDENTITY AND APPROVAL RECORD"
paragraph_001 = "Before implementation admission for native activation, a profile decision must fix: selected module version/ordinal; activation batch and historical compatibility; controller authority and rotation/revocation; supported reference formats; hot-state retention horizon; archive service/certificate protocol; historical proof/replay service retention; maximum cleanup candidates and scan work; metering/fees; reserve budgets; and exact archive storage/availability ownership."
paragraph_002 = "Proposed initial values are: at most3 blob deletions per cleanup activity, at most3 replay KV retirements, no monetary transfer, no guest execution, no newly stored content blob solely to record cleanup, and at most one fixed-size lifecycle control KV record updated in place. The fourth staged blob slot remains reserved for unavoidable real native overhead. If measured overhead cannot fit, reduce the candidate limit; do not enlarge4. Cleanup evidence lives in the canonical receipt/batch and archived certificate, not an unbounded fresh KV audit row."
paragraph_003 = "The native hot retention horizon is an UNASSIGNED profile parameter, not an invented fixed4096-batch minimum. The application claim horizon4096 does not require every obsolete native version to stay in the live table, and it is not authority to shorten historical proof availability. The owner must assign the native hot horizon against actual dispute/recovery/replay contracts and provisioned authenticated archive retrieval. Admission must prove the resulting mutation-rate times hot-window occupancy fits unchanged512slots/64MiB and512KV; otherwise the profile cannot enable continuous work. Every currently live obligation/reference remains pinned independently of age. A finalized cutoff must be derived from existing independent finality verification, never Context executing height alone, elapsed time or indexer depth."
paragraph_004 = "Historical archive retention is indefinite in this candidate. Finite retention requires an explicit later approved contract that identifies affected guarantees and users; it cannot arise from an operator deleting old archive objects. Indefinite retention means capacity planning and provisioned archive growth, not a promise of infinite hardware."
paragraph_005 = "The candidate availability certificate uses two separately administered, explicitly enrolled Ed25519 archive keys with2-of-2 signatures. This is a proposed new archive-availability trust assumption, separate from consensus/finality signers and separate from wallet custody. It must be approved or replaced by a fully specified stronger availability mechanism. A valid signature authenticates an archive operator's durable-availability claim; it does not mathematically prove perpetual storage. No unseen operational key or signing fleet is presumed."

[storage.S06]
title = "ARCHIVE COMPLETENESS BEFORE RETIREMENT"
paragraph_001 = "An archive unit binds network/genesis domain, protocol/module versions, profile version, canonical source sequence/root, receipt-state root, finalized batch/header/checkpoint identity, snapshot digest and exact byte length, ordered canonical log/batch segment digests/ranges, Programs artifact/interface versions, all program replay witnesses and metadata proofs required for the range, authority/trust-history material, and a content inventory root. All hashes use existing algorithms/encodings for existing objects; only the new manifest/certificate wrapper has its independently specified versioned domain."
paragraph_002 = "The full source snapshot must contain every committed native blob and KV required by its existing format, not just PAXAI's current state or an app event projection. Existing lxp_snapshot_write/load/root verification and lxp_snapshot_store_write/read are the starting interfaces. A snapshot cannot be fabricated by omitting old blobs while keeping its original root. Canonical logs after an archived snapshot must be complete enough to reconstruct every promised intermediate state, including exact old code/version semantics, external committed inputs and deterministic cleanup certificates."
paragraph_003 = "Existing relay archive preserves pinned bootstrap genesis/snapshot and exact raw canonical batch bytes transactionally, with contiguous batch/sequence/root checks. This provides useful raw material, but it does not establish ongoing snapshots, complete native state-proof service or every replay section's sufficiency. The new archive integration must explicitly demonstrate required replay/prestate/metadata-proof sections are in the retained bytes, or persist the missing exact sections through a versioned extension. A raw batch hash without those bytes is insufficient."
paragraph_004 = "Each archive signs only after local byte persistence, digest/length verification, existing snapshot-root verification, canonical segment continuity checks and a durable inventory transaction. The two archives compare the same immutable manifest digest, sequence/root and range. Certificates also bind archive identity generation, storage-profile digest and retention commitment. Conflicting manifests at the same immutable identity refuse; exact repeats are idempotent. Certificate issuance failure cannot authorize retirement."
paragraph_005 = "A new native maintenance call consumes exact canonical certificate bytes and pinned keys; deterministic execution never makes an HTTP request or bases validity on a transient remote health response. Operators perform downloads, independent restoration and availability checks before submission. Replicas validate the same certificate/provenance bytes under the fixed profile. Their live replay must not depend on the original archive still being reachable at that instant."

[storage.S07]
title = "EXACT LIVE-REFERENCE ACCOUNTING"
paragraph_001 = "Deletion eligibility is recomputed against the admitted current committed revision and the transaction's effective staged view. An offchain suggestion or cached refcount is never authority. Expected sequence/root mismatch refuses and requires a new immutable request; the collector does not silently collect a different candidate set."
paragraph_002 = "The reference vocabulary must cover both41-byte shared and73-byte principal/protocol storage heads, every current namespace manifest and its cell values, deployed current/upgrade/migration artifacts and interface references, live sandbox/occupancy state, active replay records and their witness digests, prepared in-flight transitions/snapshots and any other supported Programs record that can resolve a blob. Unknown reference-bearing formats, malformed manifests, unresolved dependencies or incomplete ownership information block retirement for affected candidates. An implementation must document the closed parser set for its approved profile before claiming generic collection."
paragraph_003 = "Current namespace manifests are transitive roots. A candidate value referenced by another live namespace cannot be deleted even if its first namespace no longer uses it. Identical cross-program values/manifests may deduplicate within the Programs blob domain; ownership by the submitting market does not imply exclusivity. Include all live Programs namespaces, not only the submitting program. Non-Programs blobs and unclassified Programs content are permanently pinned by candidate profile1."
paragraph_004 = "In-flight prepared transactions must be serialized with maintenance or hold exact native lifetime pins until commit/rollback. The candidate's simplest policy is no maintenance admission while a prepared dependency level or open journal is outstanding; ordinary transitions cannot race a cleanup check and then access freed data. The native integration must enforce this on the real kernel path, not merely through a keeper mutex."
paragraph_005 = "Reference counts may be maintained as a deterministic acceleration structure only if rebuilt from actual canonical state and checked against it during recovery. They cannot change existing root preimages invisibly. Per-version unbounded refcount/audit rows are forbidden. A reference-count mismatch refuses cleanup and reports corruption; no best-effort sweep is allowed."

[storage.S08]
title = "RETIREABLE CANDIDATE CLASSES AND PROVENANCE"
paragraph_001 = "Profile1 admits only two candidate classes: obsolete PAXAI namespace manifest/value versions, and historical Programs replay record/witness pairs outside the approved hot horizon with complete archive evidence. Other artifacts, arbitrary opaque blobs and unrelated application content remain pinned."
paragraph_002 = "For obsolete PAXAI versions, the request identifies the exact original program/shared namespace, original state revision, digest/size and historical receipt/root. Existing canonical state witnesses must prove the historical namespace head and its referenced manifest at the independently authenticated root. The manifest must have the declared one PAXAI shared key, name the candidate value digest/size and decode canonically. The current program must be an enrolled PAXAI artifact/profile instance; an arbitrary user cannot present a similarly named key to widen deletion authority. Historical bytes are verified with existing witness/root functions; archive operator signatures alone cannot turn unproved data into historical state."
paragraph_003 = "The candidate must exist in the current native table with matching module, digest, exact byte length and content hash. Its old origin being proven does not imply it is unreferenced now; S07's current liveness check remains mandatory. A currently used manifest/value is always protected. The source root must be strictly older than the approved finalized cutoff and covered by an immutable archive unit."
paragraph_004 = "For replay retirement, identify the exact activity-keyed replay metadata record and witness digest, original sequence/root and archived metadata proof/witness. Validate the existing replay record format, bounds and authority/network bindings. Retire the metadata KV and its content only when no live/hot obligation or other canonical reference still needs them; shared witnesses remain until the last reference retires. Do not delete only the witness and leave an unusable record. Do not claim every call emits replay capture; actual presence is part of admission/accounting."
paragraph_005 = "Retirement never alters historical metadata proofs or activity receipts. The archive must answer them against the original receipt root or reconstruct that exact historical state. Current mutable-head proof lookup cannot be passed off as the historical proof after cleanup."

[storage.S09]
title = "BOUNDED MAINTENANCE REQUEST AND RESULTS"
paragraph_001 = "The proposed request schema is versioned canonical binary, independent from PAXAI application envelope. It binds network domain, selected maintenance profile version/digest, controller principal, expected global sequence/current root, finalized cutoff/header identity, archive manifest digest/size/range, certificate bytes, up to3 sorted distinct candidate descriptors and their bounded provenance witness bytes. Candidate descriptors include class, module9, program/namespace identity where applicable, digest, exact size, origin activity/receipt/sequence/root, optional paired replay KV identity and expected live-reference disposition. Every count/length/enum has an explicit maximum; unknown trailing bytes and duplicate candidates refuse."
paragraph_002 = "Maximum request is32768 bytes for the restricted one-key PAXAI provenance profile. A larger required proof cannot be truncated or accepted by hash alone; refuse PROVENANCE_BOUND and redesign the profile under review. Existing witness encodings are reused without changing field widths or hash rules. The new wrapper is specified by the native implementation owner before implementation and bound in the profile digest."
paragraph_003 = "The response and outcome contain request identity, profile digest, actual old/new state roots, retired digest/class/bytes list, retired replay-record list, counts and byte totals before/after, archive manifest/certificate identity and a precise result. Idempotency binds the candidate set and origin evidence. A repeat after successful cleanup returns already retired only with existing canonical receipt evidence; absence by itself is not proof that the requested cleanup happened. Wrong current root, current-live reference, unavailable provenance, invalid archive certificate, unfinalized cutoff, unknown format, insufficient reserve or malformed content refuses atomically."
paragraph_004 = "Meter the bounded scan, hashing, proof validation, certificate checks and staged operations with a versioned native price/work schedule. The caller pays admitted native costs under existing fee law; no money is moved by cleanup. If the worst supported scan cannot finish under approved work/transport bounds, block that profile rather than skip reference checks."

[storage.S10]
title = "ATOMIC HEADROOM AND ADMISSION"
paragraph_001 = "The current native prepare path checks additions against precommit counts/bytes and does not credit deletions as immediate capacity. Keep that behavior unless a separately qualified change is required; a combined replace/delete call must not assume net capacity is enough. Cleanup primarily deletes, so it can restore headroom without constructing a new app value/manifest. Mandatory cleanup receipt/control overhead must fit reserved slots/bytes/KV before admitting more user work."
paragraph_002 = "Proposed conservative operator policy reserves64 blob slots and8MiB committed byte headroom globally for maintenance and already accepted terminal obligations, and at least16 native KV slots for recovery/control/replay overhead. These are initial profile policies, not proof that they cover the workload. Admission computes the larger of these minima and the measured sum of obligations already admitted. If the bound exceeds remaining capacity, refuse new epochs/work/funding before taking money. Never consume that reserve for routine expansion."
paragraph_003 = "New atomic native admission must calculate worst-case additions for the complete transition, including optional replay capture, artifact/evidence, manifests, fee/occupancy state, staged accounts, transfer legs/assets and effects. An authenticated capacity read binds counts/bytes/reserves to a committed sequence/root; it does not reserve anything. A separately serialized reservation bound to the native activity/request digest must expire/cancel/reconcile without duplication and be checked again during prepare. If not implemented, preflight remains advisory and native atomic refusal is authoritative."
paragraph_004 = "The existing guest Context has no blob-count, free-capacity or finalized-cutoff field. Do not invent guest selectors or add caller-supplied capacity as authority. The keeper/readiness adapter reads a new authenticated native capacity interface through existing private boundary conventions. UNKNOWN/STALE counts block automatic expansion. Under contention, a request can still fail capacity safely; UI and orchestration retain truthful pending/refused state."
paragraph_005 = "Retire old content proactively while adequate reserve remains. At total512slots/64MiB with all objects legitimately live/pinned, maintenance must refuse unsafe deletion and admit no new mutations requiring additions. Manual physical deletion, artificial cap enlargement, fabricated free counts or early claim/retention expiry are prohibited recovery measures."

[storage.S11]
title = "RESTART, JOURNAL, SNAPSHOT AND REPLICA CONTRACT"
paragraph_001 = "Archive publication and canonical cleanup are separate durability domains. Durable archive completion is recorded before cleanup submission. The keeper persists exact request/certificate bytes and submission identity before sending; lost response triggers receipt/current-head reconciliation. It must not assume timeout means rollback or resubmit a contradictory current-root request as a duplicate success."
paragraph_002 = "Cleanup uses the real native staged deletion/prepare/commit path. Crash before commit restores prior full table; crash after canonical commit reconstructs the new complete table and exact root. No state with missing still-live blobs is acknowledged. Existing snapshot store temporary-file, fdatasync, rename and directory-fsync semantics are preserved; a cleanup snapshot is a new snapshot with a new root/digest, never an overwritten old identity."
paragraph_003 = "Existing snapshot format includes every active native blob. Load rejects inconsistent counts/lengths/ordering/root. The live blob table after cleanup remains<=512/64MiB. Archived snapshots retain removed objects outside that table. Replay from an archived source snapshot and exact canonical history through cleanup must produce byte-identical receipts and roots with every replica executing the same approved module/profile version."
paragraph_004 = "Prepared replay checkpoints deep-copy blobs today. Preserve that lifetime independence, rollback correctness and pin semantics; do not convert them to dangling references. Root/certificate verification cannot fetch missing bytes from an unauthenticated fallback. Missing archived recovery material is an explicit recovery failure, not permission to initialize an empty app or forget liabilities."
paragraph_005 = "Independent archive restoration must rebuild all retained PAXAI state/claims/actor sequences, account-binding proofs and native balances, and verify source/target roots without relying on the keeper's cached inventory. Application payout dictionaries/refcounts and native content references are different data structures and must not be confused."

[storage.S12]
title = "HISTORICAL PROOF AND AVAILABILITY SERVICE"
paragraph_001 = "A NEW private historical-state adapter accepts exact network/root/sequence/receipt identity and bounded proof selectors. It returns original canonical snapshot/receipt/batch/witness bytes or a verifiable proof/replay reconstruction under the original authority and existing encodings. Public PAXAI views expose only permitted data and truthful availability/finality, never private archive credentials or whole confidential snapshots."
paragraph_002 = "The adapter must distinguish not retained by an explicitly approved policy, currently unavailable, invalid/corrupt archive and nonexistent selector. It cannot claim authenticated absence based only on a database miss. Old snapshot digest/root is immutable even after live cleanup. Replay metadata proof service must use the archived historical root, not the new live root."
paragraph_003 = "Archive queues, manifests, local snapshots, canonical logs and certificate issuance journals persist before advancing cursors. Both archives retain exact immutable bytes and independently test recovery. New material is not marked durable merely because a file exists or an upload returned a URL. Any archive full/unavailable/corrupt state closes retirement admission; existing live state remains intact."
paragraph_004 = "No consumer is promised new generalized historical proofs until its actual adapter and data are qualified. An existing relay raw-batch endpoint is reusable transport, not proof that this new service exists."

[storage.S13]
title = "FUTURE IMPLEMENTATION OWNERSHIP AND SINGLE GATES"
paragraph_001 = "All paths and gates below are proposed future work. All implementation and qualification tasks remain pending. Every task has implementation-first, one build plus one focused behavior gate, at mosttwo task-scoped repair cycles and30minute cap. A command naming a new target becomes runnable only when its owning task adds it; do not report these commands as current evidence."
paragraph_002 = "ai.T-S01 Archive retention and restoration contract, owner archive/storage integration. Existing exact paths: include/layerx/lxp_snapshot.h, src/state/lxp_snapshot.c, src/storage/lxp_snapshot_store.c, src/replica/lxp_replay_checkpoint.c, src/replica/lxp_history.c, platform/relay_archive/store.py, protocol.py and runtime.py. Proposed additions: platform/relay_archive/state_archive.py and tests/relay-archive/state_archive_lifecycle.py. Deliver exact immutable ongoing snapshot/log/witness inventory,2-of-2 certificate issuance with fixed profile, independent native restore and historical proof retrieval. Build target: make layerxd; current Makefile resolves it to build/bin/layerxd under default BUILD_DIR. Bind the exact revision and relevant adapters at task admission."
paragraph_003 = "Single future gate: python3 tests/relay-archive/state_archive_lifecycle.py --native-node build/bin/layerxd. It must invoke the real node/snapshot/replay/proof paths and two actual archive processes, not mock blob maps or fabricated authority. If the actual executable path differs, owner must bind the real artifact in task admission before implementation; do not weaken the gate to serializer-only checks."
paragraph_004 = "ai.T-S02 Deterministic Programs retirement, owner native Programs/storage. Requires approved profile and ai.T-S01. Existing paths: include/layerx/programs.h, include/layerx/lxp_module.h, include/layerx/lxp_kernel.h, src/modules/programs/registration.c, storage.c, state_record.c, src/protocol/lxp_module_ctx.c, src/protocol/lxp_kernel.c, src/state/lxp_state_root.c and lxp_state_proof.c. Proposed additions: src/modules/programs/blob_lifecycle.c, its private header and tests/programs/test_blob_lifecycle.c; root Makefile registers the focused binary/target. Deliver exact current-root/auth/archive/provenance/reference admission, bounded canonical deletions, replay KV retirement, deterministic outcome and no cap changes. Proposed one build: make build/tests/lxp_test_blob_lifecycle. Proposed one gate: make test-paxai-blob-lifecycle."
paragraph_005 = "The target runs that real native binary; it must not expand to aggregate suites."
paragraph_006 = "ai.T-S03 Capacity admission and keeper, owner native boundary/operator adapter. Requires ai.T-S02. Existing paths: include/layerx/lxp_kernel.h, src/protocol/lxp_kernel.c and lxp_module_ctx.c, current private LNI boundary in cmd/layerxd/lxp_daemon_lni.c and platform/hosted/authority/. Proposed service addition: platform/hosted/paxai-storage-keeper/ with exact package/manifest names assigned before admission; proposed focused test path tests/programs/test_blob_admission.c. Deliver root-bound authenticated capacity observation, serialized request reservations, reserve-aware admission, persisted keeper requests/certificates and real receipt reconciliation. Proposed one build: make build/tests/lxp_test_blob_admission."
paragraph_007 = "Proposed one gate: make test-paxai-blob-admission; task adds both targets and binds real LNI/kernel/authority rather than returning invented counters."
paragraph_008 = "ai.T-S04 PAXAI continuous-operation integration, owner app+native boundary, requires ai.T-S01..03 and app funding/claim paths. Exact proposed package programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market, actual Programs SDK and native adapters, proposed focused test tests/programs/test_paxai_storage_continuity.c plus root Makefile target. Proposed one build: make build/tests/lxp_test_paxai_storage_continuity. Proposed one gate: make test-paxai-storage-continuity. It performs more than512 distinct authoritative PAXAI mutations through real native execution, funded claim/recovery operations and repeated versioned cleanup, while all native capacities remain unchanged. Interface availability and a document parse cannot satisfy this gate."
paragraph_009 = "The task admission owner must resolve any broad-path conflict with active project ownership and the new native profile before dispatch. No native architecture work is inferred as authorized implementation by these proposed paths."

[storage.S14]
title = "REQUIRED FOCUSED ACCEPTANCE CASES"
paragraph_001 = "The retirement gate must demonstrate current shared-head protection; cross-namespace dedup protection; both41/73byte head forms; old manifest/value eligibility after authenticated archive; replay KV+witness paired retirement; malformed/unknown reference fail-closed; duplicate/conflicting candidate refusal; expected-root race refusal; wrong network/profile/key/cutoff refusal; at most3deletions within4staged entries; no unbounded per-retirement KV growth; real current root changes deterministically; old proof remains valid against original root; and monetary balances/liabilities remain untouched by maintenance."
paragraph_002 = "Archive gate must demonstrate exact original snapshot-root reconstruction, every needed replay witness/metadata proof retained, corrupt/truncated/missing segment refusal, conflicting immutable identity refusal, certificate issued only after both independent archives persist the same inventory, and recovery when one archive is unavailable without weakening certificate policy."
paragraph_003 = "Capacity gate must demonstrate no addition counted as available merely because another staged operation plans to delete; no read mistaken for reservation; two conflicting writers cannot spend the same reserve; reservation crash/retry keeps one identity; full-live/pinned store refuses without deleting live content; and pending payout/exit obligations retain reserve."
paragraph_004 = "Continuity gate must include more than512 distinct app state mutations with actual namespace finalization and replay capture where required, cleanup across multiple checkpoints, crash before/after archive persist and native commit, independent replica replay, old historical proof retrieval after deletion, live account proof consistency, funded epoch settlement and exactly-one real fixed-recipient claim after restart. It must record maximum committed count/bytes, staged entries and KV growth against unchanged512/64MiB/4/512 bounds. No repeated unchanged gate or extra confidence campaign follows a passing identified revision."

[storage.S15]
title = "PRECISE OPEN DECISIONS AND RELEASE OUTCOME"
paragraph_001 = "The existing code provides canonical staged deletion, full snapshots, durable snapshot files, raw batch archive material, existing witness verification and replay checkpoints. It does not establish a qualified generic shared-safe collector, archive availability certificate protocol, approved hot-retention profile, ongoing historical-state proof service or native reserve interface. Those are explicit new prerequisites."
paragraph_002 = "The unavoidable approval/profile decision is whether to activate a versioned Programs retirement activity with approved controller/archive authority and historical retention semantics. The next ordinal/module version, two archive operators/keys, exact hot horizon and authoritative supported-reference registry require owner assignment; deployed authority must be explicitly assigned. Until recorded and qualified, CONTINUOUS_OPERATION=BLOCKED and the only permitted advertised profile is finite capacity with honest headroom/obligation admission. This preserves current canonical hashes, replay, proofs, liabilities and native bounds without silently discarding history."
